# Changelog

All notable changes to the **Z2Z (Zimbra2Zimbra Migration Tool)** project are documented in this file.

The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/), and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html).

---

## [1.0.5] - 2026-08-27

### Added

- **Webmail Signature & Identity Migration**: Added `util/export_signatures.sh` and `util/import_signatures.sh` to export and restore user webmail signatures via `zmprov gsig` and `zmprov csig`. Plain-text (`zimbraPrefMailSignature`) and HTML (`zimbraPrefMailSignatureHTML`) variants are captured. Persona identity mappings are preserved via `gid`/`mid`.
- **Sieve Mail Filter Migration**: Added `util/export_sieve_filters.sh` and `util/import_sieve_filters.sh` to export and restore user Sieve filter scripts stored in `zimbraMailSieveScript`. Uses a temp-file approach to safely handle multi-line Sieve scripts without shell-quoting corruption. Validates target account existence before applying.
- **Out-of-Office Responder Migration**: Added `util/export_ooo.sh` and `util/import_ooo.sh` to migrate vacation auto-reply configuration including the enabled flag, message body, start date, and end date. Date attributes are validated against the required `YYYYMMDDHHMMSSZ` format before import to prevent broken UI state.
- **Calendar Resource & Equipment Migration**: Added `util/export_calendar_resources.sh` and `util/import_calendar_resources.sh` to export and provision calendar resources. Each resource manifest captures `zimbraCalResType`, capacity, contact email, and display name. Calendar data is exported as a TGZ archive via `zmmailbox` and imported with non-destructive `resolve=skip`.
- **Pre-Flight DNS Diagnostic Utility**: Added `util/dns_diagnostic.sh` to validate domain DNS records (MX, SPF, DKIM, DMARC) before migration. DKIM selectors are read automatically from `zmdkimkeyutil`. Local resolver reachability is also checked against `/etc/resolv.conf`. Outputs a color-coded diagnostic summary.
- **DKIM Key Snapshot Utility**: Added `util/export_dkim_keys.sh` to snapshot DKIM selector and public key configuration per domain. Includes a prominent advisory recommending fresh key generation on the destination server using `zmdkimkeyutil -a -d <domain>` to follow security best practices and avoid private key reuse.

### Fixed (Maintenance Pass — 2026-08-27)

- **Critical: `set -e` arithmetic abort on first account** — All `((var++))` arithmetic increments in `func.sh` (inside `execute_export_full`, `execute_export_trash`, `execute_export_junk` generator loops) and in every `util/` script (`audit_shares.sh`, `audit_forwards.sh`, `mailbox_size.sh`, `add_disclaimer.sh`) lacked `|| true`. Under `set -e`, `((0))` evaluates to exit code 1 and aborts the script on the very first iteration. Fixed by appending `|| true` to every bare `((var++))` expression throughout the codebase. The same fix was applied to the counter expressions embedded inside generated batch scripts (`script_export_FULL.sh`, `script_import_FULL.sh`, TRASH, JUNK).
- **Critical: Infinite recursion / stack overflow in interactive prompts** — Six functions in `func.sh` (`test_exec`, `enter_new_hostname`, `replace_hostname`, `export_mailboxes`, `get_export_destination`) and two in `skell/importar_ldap.sh` (`test_exec`, `test_import_admin`) used tail-call recursion for re-prompting on invalid input. An adversarial or accidental sequence of bad inputs would exhaust the call stack. Converted all to `while true` loops with `continue` for invalid input and `break`/`return`/`exit` for valid choices.
- **`portable_replace()` temp file leak on failure** — If `sed` failed (e.g. read-only filesystem), the `.tmp.XXXXXX` staging file was left behind and the original file was silently corrupted. Fixed by wrapping in an explicit `if/else` block that `rm -f`s the temp file on any `sed` or `mv` failure.
- **`export_sieve_filters.sh` trap race condition** — A `trap 'rm -f "${TMP_RAW}"' EXIT` was set and then immediately cleared (`trap - EXIT`) on every loop iteration. If the script exited abnormally mid-loop, only the final iteration's temp file would have been cleaned (because `TMP_RAW` is evaluated at trap-fire time), and after clearing, no cleanup ran at all. Replaced with a single global `_cleanup_sieve_export()` function registered once at startup.
- **`import_sieve_filters.sh` missing cleanup trap** — `TMP_SCRIPT` was created with `mktemp` inside the import loop but no `trap` was registered. If `set -e` triggered between creation and the final `rm -f`, the temp file leaked. Fixed with the same global-cleanup-function pattern.
- **`export_calendar_resources.sh` FAILED counter never incremented** — `FAILED` was declared and initialized to `0` but the calendar archive failure branch incremented `SUCCESS` instead, making `Failed: 0` always appear in the summary regardless of actual failures. Fixed to correctly increment `FAILED` on archive failure.
- **`check_mailbox()` non-numeric guard** — BSD `wc -l` emits leading whitespace; `mailbox_servers` could contain whitespace, making `((mailbox_servers > 1))` fail with a syntax error on some platforms. Added `${mailbox_servers//[^0-9]/}` stripping and a `:-0` fallback.
- **Version headers** — Updated version string from `1.0.4` to `1.0.5` in `func.sh` and `skell/importar_ldap.sh`.

### Changed

- **TODO**: Moved six pending tasks to Completed Tasks with version tag v1.0.5. Added seven new researched pending tasks covering incremental delta sync, Carbonio CE compatibility layer, imapsync integration, parallel multi-domain export, and ZCS 7 legacy attribute hardening.

---

## [1.0.4] - 2026-08-27

### Added (v1.0.4)

- **Automated Domain Migration**: Added automated export and restoration of email domains via `DOMINIOS.ldif` and companion script `create_domains.sh`, removing the manual domain creation requirement before LDAP ingestion.
- **Single-Pass Atomic LDAP Alias Export**: Replaced slow iterative loops with a single-pass LDAP query for email aliases, reducing export execution time from 30+ minutes down to seconds on large multi-thousand account deployments.
- **Anchored System Account Exclusion**: Upgraded filtering logic with anchored regex `^(virus-[^@]*|ham\.[^@]*|spam\.[^@]*|galsync[^@]*)@` to prevent false-positive exclusions of legitimate user accounts whose usernames contain the substring "admin" (e.g. `badminton@`, `sysadmin@`).
- **Flexible Mailbox Export Filters**: Added interactive selection allowing administrators to export all accounts, active accounts only (`zimbraAccountStatus=active`), or filter by a specific domain for phased rollouts.
- **Universal LDAP Connection & Credential Fallback**: Enhanced LDAP URI and credential resolvers with intelligent detection via `ldap_url`, `ldap_master_url`, or `zmlocalconfig`, ensuring seamless compatibility with LDAPS, custom LDAP ports, and multi-server environments.
- **Export Session Logging & Audit Trail**: Introduced timestamped session audit logs (`export/session-export-<timestamp>.log`) to track export status, command execution, and errors.
- **Global Configuration & MTA Snapshot**: Automatically extracts `CONFIG_GLOBAL.ldif` and generates `global_settings_snapshot.txt` containing critical server-wide attributes (relayhost, mynetworks, MTA restrictions, authentication mechanisms, GAL mode).
- **Progress-Aware Batch Script Generation**: Generated mailbox archiving scripts (`script_export_FULL.sh`, `script_import_FULL.sh`, TRASH, and JUNK) now include shebangs, strict safety flags (`set -euo pipefail`), real-time timestamped progress logging `[$(date)] Exporting [X/Y]...`, and success/failure counters.
- **Immediate Live Mailbox Export Option**: Added prompt in `z2z.sh` allowing operators to immediately trigger mailbox export in the active session.
- **Shared Folder & Resource Permissions Audit**: Added new utility `util/audit_shares.sh` to audit folder and calendar sharing permissions across all mailboxes.
- **Portable Stream Replacement**: Introduced `portable_replace()` using temporary staging files to guarantee cross-platform compatibility across GNU Linux and BSD/macOS without failing on `sed -i` syntax discrepancies.
- **Forwarding & Storage Telemetry**: Upgraded `audit_forwards.sh` to audit both administrative and web client forwarding rules alongside local delivery retention flags; enhanced `mailbox_size.sh` with non-numeric character sanitization and dynamic unit scaling (Bytes, KB, MB, GB, TB).
- **Technical Documentation & Architecture Suite**: Introduced [DOCNOTE.md](DOCNOTE.md) technical manual, overhauled [README.md](README.md) with badges, Mermaid migration flowcharts, RFC 2119 operational matrix, and verified ShellCheck and Markdownlint compliance.

---

## [1.0.3] - 2026-08-27

### Localization & Quality Improvements

- **Complete English Localization**: Fully translated all shell scripts, console feedback, interactive prompts, and documentation from Portuguese to standard English.
- **Modern ASCII Banner & Identity**: Refreshed ASCII terminal branding with **alsyundawy** art and standardized version metadata.
- **Code Hardening & ShellCheck Compliance**: Refactored helper routines, variable expansions, and sourcing patterns to achieve linter and static analysis compliance.
- **Documentation Architecture**: Rebuilt documentation with standardized headings, quickstart guides, compatibility specifications, and clean markdown structures.
- **Interactive Prompts Standardization**: Standardized all user-facing prompts (`Continue (yes/no)?`, `Replace hostname?`, `Export mailboxes?`) with consistent confirmation handling.
- **Console Output Styling**: Enhanced terminal output styling with structured color palettes for error and status markers.
- **Linter Verification**: Verified zero errors across integrated linters (`git-diff-check`, `markdownlint`, `prettier`, `shellcheck`, `shfmt`, `trufflehog`).

---

## [1.0.2] - 2024-03-15

### Multi-Server Improvements

- Added administrative pre-flight warnings for multi-server environments containing more than one active Mailbox server.

---

## [1.0.1] - 2023-11-20

### Group Distribution Updates

- Expanded distribution list LDAP export query to include `zimbraGroup` object class entries in addition to standard distribution lists.

---

## [1.0.0c] - 2022-08-10

### Hostname Compatibility

- Validated support for multi-server environments that do not require mailbox hostname replacement.

---

## [1.0.0b] - 2021-04-05

### Performance & Data Integrity

- Added `-t 0` parameter to `zmmailbox` commands to eliminate timeout limits when archiving large mailboxes (>2GB).
- Switched default mailbox import strategy from `reset` (destructive overwrite) to `skip` (safe non-destructive merge).

---

## [1.0.0a] - 2020-09-18

### Bug Fixes

- Fixed LDIF hostname comparison logic during pre-flight import checks.
- Introduced automated session logging (`session-<timestamp>.log`) to trace import operations.

---

## [0.9.9f] - 2019-12-14

### Hostname Validation

- Added strict FQDN syntax validation when interactively entering replacement hostnames.
- Enforced hostname parity validation between local Zimbra server and imported LDIF records.
- Standardized environment discovery through native Zimbra environment variables.

---

## [0.9.9c] - 2018-06-22

### Admin & System Alias Options

- Added interactive toggle allowing administrators to choose whether to export/import the `admin` user account.
- Added default alias exclusions to preserve native `root` and `postmaster` system aliases.

---

## [0.9.9] - 2017-02-10

### Initial Release

- Core export/import pipeline for user accounts and distribution lists.
- Built-in exclusion filters for internal Zimbra system accounts (spam, ham, virus quarantine, galsync).
- Batch script generation for full mailbox archive exports via `zmmailbox`.
